WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.550
Taiwan has its own elected
government, and runs its own affairs.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:09.090
The United Nations has 193 member states.

3
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:12.470
Membership grew from 51 in 1945.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.650
The newest member, South
Sudan, joined in 2011.

5
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.890
Taiwan is not one of them.

6
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:23.190
So why does a place that elects its own
government have no seat at the United

7
00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:24.430
Nations?

8
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:27.810
In this mission, you'll pin
down what makes a state,

9
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.190
a nation and a nation state.

10
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.930
Then you'll map borders that
are made, split and argued over,

11
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.310
from Ukraine to East Asia.

12
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:41.070
Your mission: explain why Taiwan
has no seat at the United Nations,

13
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.080
though it elects its own government.
